Tricky Interview Question of DevOps:

Difference between Kubectl create and Kubectl apply?

🔹 1. kubectl create:- 

👉 Purpose: Create a resource only once.

Key Points:
• Creates a new resource from a YAML/JSON file.
•❌ Fails if the resource already exists
Does not track changes.

Example Command:

kubectl create -f deployment.yaml

Behavior:
First time → ✅ Success
Second time → ❌ Error (Already exists)

🔹 2. kubectl apply:-

👉 Purpose: Create or update resources (Declarative way)

Key Points:
• Can create + update existing resources.
• Keeps track of changes using last-applied-configuration.
•Supports declarative approach

Example Command:

kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml

Behavior:
First time → ✅ Creates resource
Next time → 🔄 Updates only changed fields
